    answer: "The direct answer is that true \"stamp only\" — a PE applying their seal to drawings they have not reviewed — is not a legitimate service in any state. Every state board requires the sealing engineer to be in responsible charge of the work: Texas through TBPELS Rule 137.33, California through Business & Professions Code 6735, Florida through 61G15, Arizona through its Board of Technical Registration rules. A seal without review violates those rules, exposes the PE to discipline up to license revocation, and leaves the owner holding drawings whose certification is worthless. When someone searches for \"stamp only,\" what they actually need — and what legitimate firms provide — is review-and-seal.\n\nReview-and-seal is the compliant version of what the search term is reaching for. The PE takes responsible charge of the drawing set: reviews it completely, independently verifies the engineering and calculations, marks the revisions the design needs, confirms the corrections, and then seals. The drawings get sealed — that part of the request is honored — but the seal certifies engineering the PE actually evaluated. For a client with an already-drawn set, this is usually faster and less expensive than full redesign, because the PE is verifying and correcting rather than starting from zero. But the review is real, and any firm that tells you otherwise is telling you they will break the rules for a fee.\n\nI want to be direct about the red flags, because they cost owners real money. A PE who promises a same-day seal with no review, who does not ask for your calculations or basis of design, who seals a discipline outside their competence, or whose fee is a flat number with no questions asked — that is not efficiency, that is a board complaint waiting to happen. And the owner's exposure is not theoretical: unreviewed sealed drawings that fail in the field trace liability back through the seal to a PE who never did the engineering, and the owner's project sits on a certification no board would defend. Legitimate review-and-seal protects everyone in the chain, starting with you.",
